The project only defines `bun test` in `package.json` (no separate typecheck/lint), so that was the only check run.

Committed on `work/main` in two commits:

- `dee262a` Run queued jobs sequentially and asynchronously
- `a7edb2a` Add tests for queue ordering, errors, and draining

One decision worth flagging: `drain` still returns immediately when the queue is empty at the moment it's called, even if a job is pushed synchronously on the very next line. That matches the documented "every job pushed so far" semantics, but if you want a drain call to also cover jobs pushed in that same synchronous tick, I can make it yield once before checking.

